{
  "title": "77: al-Mursalaat المرسلات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالْمُرْسَلٰتِ عُرْفًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAL MURSALAATE U’URFAN.\nBy the (Winds) sent forth one after another (to man's profit); \nفَالْعٰصِفٰتِ عَصْفًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL A’AASEFAATE A’ASFAN.\nWhich then blow violently in tempestuous Gusts, \nوَّالنّٰشِرٰتِ نَشْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nWWAALNNAASHERAATE NASHRAN.\nAnd scatter (things) far and wide; \nفَالْفٰرِقٰتِ فَرْقًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAL FAAREQAATE FARQAN.\nThen separate them, one from another, \nفَالْمُلْقِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(5)\nFAL MULQEETE ZIKRAA.\nThen spread abroad a Message, \nعُذْرًا اَوْ نُذْرًا ۙ‏(6)\nU’UZRAN AW NUZRAN.\nWhether of Justification or of Warning;- \nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(7)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOON LAWAAQEA’UN.\nAssuredly, what ye are promised must come to pass. \nفَاِذَا النُّجُوْمُ طُمِسَتْۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAA NOJOOMUN TUMESAT.\nThen when the stars become dim; \nوَ اِذَا السَّمَآءُ فُرِجَتْۙ‏(9)\nWA EZAA SAMAAA-O FUREJAT.\nWhen the heaven is cleft asunder; \nوَاِذَا الْجِبَالُ نُسِفَتْۙ‏(10)\nWA EZAA JEBAALO NUSEFAT.\nWhen the mountains are scattered (to the winds) as dust; \nوَاِذَا الرُّسُلُ اُقِّتَتْؕ‏(11)\nWA EZAA ROSOLO AUQQETAT.\nAnd when the messengers are (all) appointed a time (to collect);- \nلِاَىِّ يَوْمٍ اُجِّلَتْؕ‏(12)\nLE-AYYE YAWMIN AUJJELAT.\nFor what Day are these (portents) deferred? \nلِيَوْمِ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ‏(13)\nLE-YAWMIL FASLE.\nFor the Day of Sorting out. \nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِؕ‏(14)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD AL-FASLE.\nAnd what will explain to thee what is the Day of Sorting out? \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(15)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nاَلَمْ نُهْلِكِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nALAM NUHLEKE AWWALEEN.\nDid We not destroy the men of old (for their evil)? \nثُمَّ نُتْبِعُهُمُ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ‏(17)\nSUMMA NUTBEU’UHUMU AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nSo shall We make later (generations) follow them. \nكَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(18)\nKAZAALEKA NAFA’ALU BE-MUJREMEEN.\nThus do We deal with men of sin. \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nاَلَمْ نَخْلُقْكُّمْ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍۙ‏(20)\nALAM NAKHLUQKKUM MIM MAAA-IN MMAHEENIN.\nHave We not created you from a fluid (held) despicable? \nفَجَعَلْنٰهُ فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍۙ‏(21)\nFA-JA-A’LNAAHO FEE QARAARIN MMAKEENIN.\nThe which We placed in a place of rest, firmly fixed, \nاِلٰى قَدَرٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(22)\nELAA QADARIN MA’LOOM.\nFor a period (of gestation), determined (according to need)? \nفَقَدَرْنَاۖ فَنِعْمَ الْقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(23)\nFAQADARNAA FA NE’MA AL-QAADEROONA.\nFor We do determine (according to need); for We are the best to determine (things). \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(24)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day! to the Rejecters of Truth! \nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ كِفَاتًا ۙ‏(25)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA KEFAATAN.\nHave We not made the earth (as a place) to draw together. \nاَحْيَآءً وَّاَمْوَاتًا ۙ‏(26)\nAAHYAAAN WWAAMWAATAN.\nThe living and the dead, \nوَّجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ شٰمِخٰتٍ وَّ اَسْقَيْنٰكُمْ مَّآءً فُرَاتًا ؕ‏(27)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA JA-A’LA SHAAMEKHAATIN WA AASQAYNAAKUM MMAAAN FURAATAN.\nAnd made therein mountains standing firm, lofty (in stature); and provided for you water sweet (and wholesome)? \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(28)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى مَا كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(29)\nAENTALEQOOA ELAA MAA KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\n(It will be said:) “Depart ye to that which ye used to reject as false! \nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى ظِلٍّ ذِىْ ثَلٰثِ شُعَبٍۙ‏(30)\nAENTALEQOOA ELAA ZELLIN ZEE SALAASE SHUA’ABIN.\n“Depart ye to a Shadow (of smoke ascending) in three columns, \nلَّا ظَلِيْلٍ وَّلَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ اللَّهَبِؕ‏(31)\nLAA ZALEELIN WA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL AL-LAHABE.\n“(Which yields) no shade of coolness, and is of no use against the fierce Blaze. \nاِنَّهَا تَرْمِىْ بِشَرَرٍ كَالْقَصْرِ‌ۚ‏(32)\nINNAHAA TARMEAA BESHARARIN KAALQASRE.\n“Indeed it throws about sparks (huge) as Forts, \nكَاَنَّهٗ جِمٰلَتٌ صُفْرٌ ؕ‏(33)\nKA-ANNAHU JEMAALATUN SUFRUN.\n“As if there were (a string of) yellow camels (marching swiftly).” \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(34)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nهٰذَا يَوْمُ لَا يَنْطِقُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD LAA YANTEQOON.\nThat will be a Day when they shall not be able to speak. \nوَلَا يُؤْذَنُ لَهُمْ فَيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA LAA YUZANU LAHUM FAYAA’TAZEROONA.\nNor will it be open to them to put forth pleas. \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(37)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ جَمَعْنٰكُمْ وَالْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(38)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD FASLE JAMAA’NAAKUM WA AWWALEEN.\nThat will be a Day of Sorting out! We shall gather you together and those before (you)! \nفَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ كَيْدٌ فَكِيْدُوْنِ‏(39)\nFA-IN KAANA LAKUM KAYDUN FAKEEDOONE.\nNow, if ye have a trick (or plot), use it against Me! \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(40)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ ظِلٰلٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(41)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE ZELAALIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nAs to the Righteous, they shall be amidst (cool) shades and springs (of water). \nوَّفَوَاكِهَ مِمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nWWAFAWAAKEHA MIMMAA YASHTAHOON.\nAnd (they shall have) fruits, all they desire. \nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِيْٓئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEEAN BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n“Eat ye and drink ye to your heart's content: for that ye worked (Righteousness). \nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(44)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus do We certainly reward the Doers of Good. \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(45)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nكُلُوْا وَتَمَتَّعُوْا قَلِيْلًا اِنَّكُمْ مُّجْرِمُوْنَ‏(46)\nKOLOO WATAMATTAU’OOA QALEELAA INNAKUM MUJREMOON.\n(O ye unjust!) Eat ye and enjoy yourselves (but) a little while, for that ye are Sinners. \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(47)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ ارْكَعُوْا لَا يَرْكَعُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUL ARKAU’OOA LAA YARKAU’OONA.\nAnd when it is said to them, “Prostrate yourselves!” they do not so. \nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(49)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nAh woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth! \nفَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَهٗ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(50)\nFABE-AYYE HADEESIN BAA’DAH YOAMENOON.\nThen what Message, after that, will they believe in? ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mursalaat (The Emissaries)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 50 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will not be counted from the polytheists. He will always be victorious over his enemy.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that drinking this Surah after it is written, and then dissolved in water that is mixed with the water from an onion, acts as a cure from aches and pains. Keeping this Surah, written on deerskin, as a talisman, enables one to reduce the amount of time he sleeps and he will be able to stay awake for a longer time."
}
